`lhs` is created with dims `("x", "y")` and data shape `(2, 3)`. `rhs` is created with dims `("z", "y")` and data shape `(4, 3)`. In `xr.apply_ufunc(...)`, both inputs declare `"y"` as the core dimension, so `"y"` stays as the output core dimension of length 3, while the non-core dimensions `"x"` and `"z"` broadcast together, giving lengths 2 and 4. Therefore `out.data.shape` is `[2, 4, 3]`, which the test also assigns to `observed_data_shape` and asserts.

## Answer
{"data_shape":[2,4,3]}
